<settings>
    <!--
      The phone-side editor, for people who prefer a phone keyboard to a watch
      bezel. The surface is also on the watch (settings page, or MENU), because
      it is situational: you change it when you arrive at the ski hill, not
      when you install the app. Both routes write the same Application.
      Properties store, so neither shadows the other. Any surface other than
      grass resets at local midnight.

      The labels here are duplicated in source/UvSettings.mc, which is what the
      on-watch menu draws. Loading them through Rez instead would cost a
      loadResource call per draw in the glance and hand back a Resource the
      strict checker will not pass to a String parameter. If you change one,
      change both.

      Test these from the IDE's App Settings Editor, not the simulator's own
      File menu - the simulator-side editor has a long-standing bug where it
      ignores listEntry values, and the setting here is a list.
    -->
    <setting propertyKey="@Properties.surface" title="@Strings.SurfaceTitle" prompt="@Strings.SurfacePrompt">
        <settingConfig type="list">
            <listEntry value="0">@Strings.SurfaceGrass</listEntry>
            <listEntry value="1">@Strings.SurfaceConcrete</listEntry>
            <listEntry value="2">@Strings.SurfaceWater</listEntry>
            <listEntry value="3">@Strings.SurfaceSand</listEntry>
            <listEntry value="4">@Strings.SurfaceOldSnow</listEntry>
            <listEntry value="5">@Strings.SurfaceFreshSnow</listEntry>
        </settingConfig>
    </setting>
</settings>
